---

<Docs
  title="MCP integration"
  description="Connect an AI client to x-web's hosted MCP search tool; its Standard, Deep Research or Automatic mode follows your Dashboard preference."
  toc={toc}
  updated="October 2026"
>
  <p>
    x-web provides a hosted <strong>Model Context Protocol (MCP)</strong> server. An MCP-compatible
    AI client can call x-web's live web search tool directly, without you writing an adapter or
    running a local MCP package.
  </p>

  <h2 id="quick-connect">Quick connect</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Sign in to your <a href="/dashboard">x-web dashboard</a> and create an x-web API key.</li>
    <li>Save at least one search-provider key in the dashboard. To have x-web synthesize answers with an AI model, also save your own AI provider key.</li>
    <li>In your MCP client, add the remote server URL <code>https://YOUR-X-WEB-HOST/api/mcp</code>.</li>
    <li>Set the request header <code>Authorization: Bearer YOUR_XWEB_API_KEY</code>, then connect.</li>
  </ol>
  <Callout type="note" title="Use your deployment host">
    Replace <code>YOUR-X-WEB-HOST</code> with the domain where you use x-web. For the active feature
    Preview, the MCP endpoint is <code>https://x-web-git-arena-59d33b78-x-web-flux-cf70.vercel.app/api/mcp</code>.
    Keep your API key private and configure it in the client’s secret/header settings.
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="client-config">Client configuration</h2>
  <p>
    For a client that accepts remote Streamable HTTP MCP servers and custom headers, use the server
    URL and bearer header above. A Cursor-style JSON configuration looks like this; put your actual
    x-web key in the client’s secure settings rather than committing it to a shared project:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock lang="json" title="mcp.json" code={clientConfig} />
  <p>
    In Claude Desktop or another client, add x-web as a remote MCP connector if that client version
    supports remote Streamable HTTP servers and custom authorization headers. Client setup screens
    differ; do not install an unrelated package or paste your API key into a public prompt.
  </p>

  <h2 id="tool">Available tool</h2>
  <p>
    The server exposes <code>xweb_search</code>. Give it a question or topic; it returns a grounded
    answer when available, citations, source links, the search providers used and the effective
    query. Optional inputs let the client limit the results, choose a search provider, or set the
    answer language.
  </p>
  <p>
    The endpoint uses MCP Streamable HTTP and requires your x-web account key as a bearer token on
    each request. It is stateless, so clients do not need a separate session setup.
  </p>

  <h2 id="modes">Search modes</h2>
  <p>Choose <strong>Automatic</strong>, <strong>Standard</strong> or <strong>Deep Research</strong> once in your Dashboard. The connected <code>xweb_search</code> tool automatically follows that saved preference—there is no mode field to code or configure in the agent. Automatic keeps routine lookups lightweight and escalates research-heavy questions; Standard returns quick snippets from one provider; Deep Research plans multiple queries, searches configured providers, reads up to 10 public pages, and returns a cited Markdown report. Deep mode requires the account's saved AI BYOK key; x-web never uses a server-managed model.</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="json" title="xweb_search input" code={`{ "query": "Compare the current leading video editors" }`} />

  <h2 id="credentials">Required credentials</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>x-web API key:</strong> authenticates your account and records usage.</li>
    <li><strong>Search-provider key:</strong> saved in your dashboard; powers live web search.</li>
    <li><strong>AI-provider key:</strong> optional in standard mode, but required for AI-generated answers and mandatory in deep mode. x-web never substitutes a server-owned model key.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Without an AI key, standard mode can still return live search results and any answer provided by the
    search provider; deep mode rejects the request. x-web does not call an AI model as a fallback. See the
    <a href="/docs/providers">provider guide</a> for supported search providers.
  </p>

  <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Create a separate x-web API key for each client and revoke it from your dashboard if it is lost.</li>
    <li>Store the key in the MCP client’s secret/header configuration, not source control or a shared chat.</li>
    <li>x-web validates the key on every request and loads only the credentials saved to that account.</li>
    <li>The search tool is read-only; it does not take actions on websites or access private pages.</li>
  </ul>
</Docs>
